        {
          "url": "https://resy.com/cities/san-francisco-ca/venues/camino-alto",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-30T22:59:44.156Z",
          "quote": "We love spontaneity, so we'll always keep a slug of seats for first come, first served.\n\nNo seed, or processed oils.  Animals are pasture raised, vegetables are grown in rich dark soil.  Our unique and thoughtfully managed wines are so very good.  Let's eat!  \n\nAlso, open for daytime counter service Friday to Sunday, from 9:00 to 2:30 with St. Frank coffee to go with your blueberry masa waffle...  or market salad.  No reservation needed (or taken)!"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://resy.com/cities/san-francisco-ca/venues/camino-alto",
          "observedAt": "2026-09-30T22:59:44.156Z",
          "quote": "A neighborhood restaurant using a wood burning oven to turn seasonal ingredients into beautifully simple dishes.  We start with just the good stuff, add some meticulously curated wines and a whole lotta village kindness.\nGreat meals start with great farmers, roasters, brewers and winemakers who understand Mother Earth and her seasons like few do.  Eat what you love.  Do it with thought, do it with the season, and whenever you can, do it with others."
        }
      ],
